# guard-b allowlist — one grep -E pattern per line, matched against the full
# ANNOTATED violation string:
#
#     <file>:<line>:<content>  [rule: <RULE_ID> — <description>]
#
# so an entry can be scoped to a file AND a rule AND the specific content.
#
# RULES FOR THIS FILE (adopted 2026-08-07):
#   1. No blanket `<file>:.*` entries. A whole-file exemption in a leak guard
#      disables the guard for that file — six of them were live before this
#      date and hid every rule, including the tracker-ID rules, in six ADRs.
#   2. Anchor with ^, name the file, and scope to a rule with `\[rule: ID`.
#   3. Where the exemption exists for specific identifiers, list them
#      explicitly so a *new* one is not silently inherited.
#   4. Say what the entry protects and why, in a comment above it.

# --- guard-b's own rule table -------------------------------------------------
# The RULES array literally contains the strings it scans for. Scoped to the
# rule-definition line shape ("  'RULE_ID|flags|…'"), so prose, comments and
# any other line in the script are still scanned.
^scripts/guard-b-lint\.sh:[0-9]+:  '[A-Z_]+\|[-i]\|

# --- guard-b's self-test samples ---------------------------------------------
# The self-test asserts each rule fires, so it must contain one real sample of
# each banned shape. Scoped to the sample-invocation lines only; the rest of
# the file (comments, harness code) is still scanned.
^scripts/guard-b-lint-selftest\.sh:[0-9]+:expect_(flagged|clean)

# --- ADR author attribution ---------------------------------------------------
# "Mark Kropf (Rensei)" on an ADR Authors: line is parent-company attribution.
^ADR-.*\.md:[0-9]+:\*\*Authors:\*\*.*Mark Kropf \(Rensei\)

# --- BOUNDARY-SYNC marker id --------------------------------------------------
# The synchronized-section marker id encodes the boundary concept name and must
# be globally unique across both corpora; renaming it requires a paired commit
# in the sibling corpus. It is an identifier, not a brand reference.
^001-layered-execution-model\.md:[0-9]+:.*001-donmai-rensei-platform-contract
^BOUNDARY\.md:[0-9]+:.*001-donmai-rensei-platform-contract
^scripts/check-boundary-sync\.sh:[0-9]+:.*001-donmai-rensei-platform-contract

# --- The "donmai <-> Rensei Platform contract" section heading + cross-refs ----
# The load-bearing boundary section heading names the enterprise product.
# Renaming it requires a paired commit to the sibling corpus (BOUNDARY-SYNC).
^001-layered-execution-model\.md:[0-9]+:.*(agentfactory|donmai).*Rensei Platform contract
^BOUNDARY\.md:[0-9]+:.*(agentfactory|donmai).*Rensei Platform contract
^AGENTS\.md:[0-9]+:.*(agentfactory|donmai).*Rensei Platform contract
^README\.md:[0-9]+:.*(agentfactory|donmai).*Rensei Platform contract
^ADR-template\.md:[0-9]+:.*(agentfactory|donmai).*Rensei Platform contract

# --- Parent-brand attribution in the boundary//meta docs ----------------------
# These describe the OSS<->enterprise seam and legitimately name the enterprise
# product. Scoped to the brand rule and to the specific noun phrases used.
^BOUNDARY\.md:[0-9]+:.*Rensei(-| SaaS| team| org| Platform| runs).*\[rule: BRAND_NAME
^README\.md:[0-9]+:.*Rensei(-| SaaS| team| Platform| Architecture).*\[rule: BRAND_NAME
^ADR-template\.md:[0-9]+:.*Rensei(-| team| org).*\[rule: BRAND_NAME
^001-layered-execution-model\.md:[0-9]+:.*Rensei(-| team| org| Platform).*\[rule: BRAND_NAME
^AGENTS\.md:[0-9]+:.*Rensei(-| team| org| Platform).*\[rule: BRAND_NAME

# --- Sibling closed corpus is named as a path, which contains "rensei-platform"
# `rensei-architecture/…-platform-extensions.md` cross-refs are explicitly
# allowed in this corpus; the CLOSED_PLATFORM rule matches the substring.
^(001-layered-execution-model|BOUNDARY)\.md:[0-9]+:.*rensei-architecture.*\[rule: CLOSED_PLATFORM

# --- ADR-2026-06-02-oss-brand-neutral-runtime-contract.md ---------------------
# WAS: whole-file `.*`.
# PROTECTS: the de-brand ADR enumerates, by necessity, the exact closed-source
# names it is removing — the RENSEI_* env vars, the parent domain, the closed
# TUI repo, the internal monorepo path, and the brand itself.
# NARROWED TO: those five rules. Tracker IDs, tracker URLs, tracker slugs and
# developer absolute paths in this file are NOT exempt and now fail the guard.
^ADR-2026-06-02-oss-brand-neutral-runtime-contract\.md:[0-9]+:.*\[rule: (BRAND_NAME|CLOSED_TUI_REPO|PARENT_DOMAIN|CLOSED_ENV_VAR|PLATFORM_PATH)

# --- ADR-2026-06-03-injectable-state-dir.md -----------------------------------
# WAS: whole-file `.*`.
# PROTECTS: documents the OSS<->closed composition seam for the daemon state
# dir; names the closed TUI repo and the brand to state which side owns what.
# NARROWED TO: those two rules only.
^ADR-2026-06-03-injectable-state-dir\.md:[0-9]+:.*\[rule: (BRAND_NAME|CLOSED_TUI_REPO)

# --- ADR-2026-06-01-code-survival-pool-execution.md ---------------------------
# WAS: whole-file `.*`.
# PROTECTS: two tracker lane IDs the design doc cites, plus one closed-side
# contract path it is replacing.
# NARROWED TO: those exact two IDs and that exact path. A new tracker ID in
# this file now fails the guard.
^ADR-2026-06-01-code-survival-pool-execution\.md:[0-9]+:.*\bREN-(1247|1554)\b.*\[rule: TRACKER_ID
^ADR-2026-06-01-code-survival-pool-execution\.md:[0-9]+:.*platform/src/lib/factory/code-survival-scan-contract\.ts.*\[rule: PLATFORM_PATH

# --- ADR-2026-06-02-interactive-agent-run-mode.md -----------------------------
# WAS: whole-file `.*`.
# PROTECTS: two tracker lane IDs and two parent-brand mentions naming the
# closed product whose interview lane motivates the ADR.
# NARROWED TO: those exact two IDs and those two brand phrases.
^ADR-2026-06-02-interactive-agent-run-mode\.md:[0-9]+:.*\bREN-(1563|1570)\b.*\[rule: TRACKER_ID
^ADR-2026-06-02-interactive-agent-run-mode\.md:[0-9]+:.*Rensei('s| lane).*\[rule: BRAND_NAME

# --- ADR-2026-06-03-batch-work-type-category.md -------------------------------
# WAS: whole-file `.*`.
# PROTECTS: two tracker lane IDs naming the workloads that motivate the
# batch generalization.
# NARROWED TO: those exact two IDs.
^ADR-2026-06-03-batch-work-type-category\.md:[0-9]+:.*\bREN-(1166|1265)\b.*\[rule: TRACKER_ID

# --- Parent-brand attribution in individual ADRs ------------------------------
# Each names the enterprise product once, to state which side of the boundary
# owns the behaviour. Scoped per file to the brand rule.
^ADR-2026-05-12-cli-linear-proxy\.md:[0-9]+:.*\[rule: BRAND_NAME
^ADR-2026-05-12-cross-process-hook-bus-bridge\.md:[0-9]+:.*\[rule: BRAND_NAME

# --- This file's own pattern lines --------------------------------------------
# Every entry above quotes the string it exempts, so the allowlist trips its own
# rules. Scoped to lines that are a pattern (start with ^) or a comment (start
# with #), AND to the three rules those quotes actually involve. A tracker ID, a
# tracker URL, a tracker slug or a developer absolute path in this file is still
# a violation — which is why the ADR entries above factor issue numbers as
# `REN-(1247|1554)` rather than writing the IDs literally.
^\.guard-allowlist:[0-9]+:[#^].*\[rule: (BRAND_NAME|CLOSED_PLATFORM|PLATFORM_PATH)
